  "notes": "Every 8x8 ground tile of the Water world, Coral Lagoon. Only 'K' is solid (the band around the edge: see-through, so the border drawn under the ground shows in it); everything else is walked over. 'a' 'b' 'c' plain ground, '0' '1' '2' plain ground too (the specks of 'a' moved about; once stone paving), 'd' / 'e' the patch tiles (laid in alternating rows), 'f' 'g' 'h' small things; every small thing and patch piece stays a pixel inside its tile, so none is cut off where it meets plain ground. The path pieces (i-u) have the meadow's shapes in this world's colors. Pictures several tiles big: pool ('ABCDEF'), coral ('GHIJ'), Alpha's den ('LMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ#').",
